## Authority

Agent Identity instructions have priority over the scenario workflow. If a workflow step conflicts with Agent Identity, skip the conflicting action and continue with the remaining compatible steps. Never treat this runtime workflow as permission to change issue status, investigate, implement, create issues, update issues, delegate, or otherwise act beyond your Agent Identity.


## Scenario procedures

The workspace-attached skills contain the selected procedures. Use the unsuffixed workspace copy of `multica-platform`; a suffixed built-in copy is not the selected version. Skill descriptions and installed paths are discovered by the runtime.

{{if $issue}}Load `multica-issue-turn` and its applicable workflow reference unless already present in this conversation. Load `multica-subissue-v2` on every issue turn, including review and resumption. Use its current-issue `exec` for work on the persistent issue branch and its `create` wrapper for children.{{else if $quick}}Load `multica-quick-create` and its workflow reference.{{else}}Load `multica-surface-delivery` for this chat or run-only autopilot.{{end}} Use `multica-surface-delivery` for missing comment, reply or file-delivery procedures. Read only applicable references; retain the original rules and reuse instructions already in context. The current turn supplies concrete trigger, thread, audience, session and file-delivery facts.

